---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Tools · Using-IT" description="Free web tools built for daily IT work: timecalc, session time counter and Edge Bookmarks Creator.">
  <section class="article-hero wrap">
    <div class="kicker">Tools</div>
    <h1>Small tools, built for daily IT work</h1>
    <div class="article-meta">Free · browser-based · no account needed</div>
  </section>
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <p>Over the years I have built a handful of small tools that make everyday IT work a little easier. They live here on using-it.dk: free to use, no strings attached.</p>

    <h2>Timecalc: work hours calculator</h2>
    <p>Enter your start and end times, subtract lunch and breaks, and see the day's total working time at a glance.</p>
    <p><a class="btn-primary" href="/timecalc/timecalc.html">Open Timecalc →</a></p>

    <h2>Time Counter: target time tracker</h2>
    <p>Set a target time, subtract 30 minutes for lunch automatically, and keep an eye on the balance for the day. Originally built for a colleague who wanted the "am I done yet?" question answered.</p>
    <p><a class="btn-primary" href="/timecalc/BO.html">Open Time Counter →</a></p>

    <h2>Edge Bookmarks Creator</h2>
    <p>Build Microsoft Edge Managed Favorites structures visually and export JSON ready for Intune deployment. Read the full story in <a href="/build-microsoft-edge-managed-favorites-with-a-gui/">Build Microsoft Edge Managed Favorites with a GUI</a>.</p>
    <p><a class="btn-primary" href="/tools-2/">Open the tools page →</a></p>

    <h2>More</h2>
    <p>I link to third-party tools I use most on the <a href="/tools-2/">tools page</a>, and occasionally demo tools on my <a href="/youtube/">YouTube channel</a>.</p>
    <p>Have an idea for a tool that would save you time? <a href="/about-me/">Reach out</a>: several of these were born from a coffee break conversation.</p>
  </div>
</Base>